course: dictionary
lesson: 6085
title: Metaphors: saying one thing is another
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A metaphor says one thing IS another thing, to show what it is like. It does not use «like» or «as». «The classroom was a zoo» does not mean the room had animals in it. It means the room was wild and noisy.
explain: Compare a simile. «The sun is like a golden coin» uses like, so it is a simile. «The sun is a golden coin» says it IS one, so it is a metaphor. Both help you see what the two things share: round, shiny and gold.
explain: To spot a metaphor, ask: is the writer saying one thing IS another, and would the sentence be false if you read it word for word? If so, it is probably a metaphor. Then ask what the two things have in common.
explain: Metaphors are everywhere. «A sea of faces» and «a storm of applause» are hidden metaphors, and so is «my room is a pigsty». Writers use metaphors to make their own writing vivid.
fact: A metaphor says one thing is another, to show what the two things share.
fact: «Time is money» and «He has a heart of stone» are both metaphors.
fact: A simile uses «like» or «as»; a metaphor does not.
fact: A metaphor can also be a thing or idea that stands for something else: a journey can be a metaphor for growing up.
fact: «A night owl» is a metaphor for someone who stays up late.
exercise: «The classroom was a zoo.» What does this metaphor show? | *The room was wild and noisy | The room had lots of animals in it | The room was very quiet and tidy | The room was painted green
exercise: Which one is a metaphor, not a simile? | *«The sun is a golden coin» | «The sun shone as bright as a coin» | «The sun was hot» | «The sun is like a golden coin»
exercise: Which phrase is a hidden metaphor? | The sea was calm | The waves rolled in | A bright blue sky | *a sea of faces
test: Jayden writes «My brother is a tornado at breakfast.» What does this metaphor mean? | *He is wild and messy at breakfast | He is a weather forecaster | He is a real tornado that blew the door open | He eats very little at breakfast
test: Which sentence is a metaphor? | She runs like the wind | He was as tall as a tree | *Her eyes were stars | The dog barked loudly
exam: Which word in a simile is a clue that it compares two things? | blue | big | river | *like
